8db7834aaba022c3a8251612c5cb1f018164751a15"}},"query":"The 22 May riots in Panama against President de la Guardia's administration have led him to declare a state of siege and may erupt into full-scale revolution. The strong national guard, whose repression of student demonstrations earlier this week resulted in one death and widespread and violent resentment, has announced that it is slowly re-gaining control of Panama City. The guard has orders to kill. The students have been joined in a general strike against the government by labor unions and other groups, but appear to have lost control of the disturbance to hoodlums. The latter are probably incited by powerful opposition politicians [REDACTION] who are trying to oust the President. Similar riots are occurring in Colon, the northern terminus of the canal.","query_utf8_sha256":"43ad9d3a64bee57cfa5e23769dc476653658ca053096a1ec2602c0296052c6bf","source_assessment":{"display_reading_id":"next_reading_d05a2b3d020d8f566482c1e9","method_id":"source_realized_redaction_v1","readings":[{"candidates":[{"evidence_state":"INFERENTIAL_CONTEXT","fill":"such as former President Harmodio Arias","priority":0.41547284644194754,"rank":1},{"evidence_state":"INFERENTIAL_CONTEXT","fill":"such as First Vice President Diaz","priority":0.41472672241093983,"rank":2}],"reading_id":"next_reading_d05a2b3d020d8f566482c1e9"},{"candidates":[{"evidence_state":"INFERENTIAL_CONTEXT","fill":"such as former President Harmodio Arias","priority":0.41547284644194754,"rank":1},{"evidence_state":"INFERENTIAL_CONTEXT","fill":"such as First Vice President Diaz","priority":0.41472672241093983,"rank":2}],"reading_id":"next_reading_1a005fb20ea90c8bede96ba7"},{"candidates":[{"evidence_state":"INFERENTIAL_CONTEXT","fill":"like former President Harmodio Arias","priority":0.4211037988229,"rank":1}],"reading_id":"next_reading_fa2b9f6ac0c608a3525d0515"}],"source_documents":["CIA-RDP79T00975A003200190001-5","CIA-RDP79T00975A003600250001-4"]},"task":"redaction"},{"a